🔑 MAIN CONCEPT LEARNED
Method Chaining (Fluent Interface Pattern) ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

This is the biggest takeaway from this code.

Example usage:
new Calculator(10)
  .add(5)
  .multiply(2)
  .subtract(4)
  .getResult();   // 26

Why it works?

Each method returns:

return this;


📌 Concept:

this refers to the current object

Returning this allows the next method call on the same instance

🧠 Interview one-liner:

Method chaining allows multiple operations to be executed in a single expression by returning the object itself.

